Theorem VF-8: stack applies to ALL rules including unimplemented sec-8 and target-only surface

  Preconditions:
    - VF-8 governs the universal-coverage mandate per Annex E §AIMS VF-8:
      "Stack applies to ALL rules — incl. unimplemented sec-8 rules.
      Unimplemented rule without verification layer planned = spec gap." The
      sec-01 Verification.proof restates: "verification stack applies to ALL
      rules — incl. unimplemented sec-8 rules + target-only sec-1.5 / IC-3 /
      IC-5 surface."
    - VF-8's concrete shape is Rule -> Bool per
      aims-proof/proofs/01-verification/Verification.proof. Discharged here
      against the sec-01 Verification.proof sorry obligation.
    - Coverage applies to three rule classes: (1) implemented rules (carry an
      ACTIVE verification layer — e.g. sec-8 RL-1..RL-5 covered by VF-1 / VF-4);
      (2) unimplemented sec-8 rules (RL-22 through RL-26 post-pipeline, covered
      by a PLANNED VF-7 three-tier layer); (3) target-only surface (sec-1.5
      ArgEscaping, IC-3 ParamContract, IC-5 EffectSummary — covered by a PLANNED
      VF-2 (b)/(c)/(d) layer via RL-29 / RL-30 / RL-31). An unimplemented rule
      with NO planned layer is a SPEC GAP.
    - TARGET-ONLY whole-stack mandate: there is no single shipped verifier
      function — VF-8 is the coverage invariant the verification stack asserts
      across all rules. conformance: target-only.
    - depends-on sec-08: the unimplemented RL-22..RL-26 + the target-only
      RL-29/RL-30/RL-31 LLVM-fact-export rules whose planned layers VF-8
      requires.

  Soundness property:
    Forall rule R in the AIMS ruleset:

      (P1) Universal coverage: R is covered by the verification stack IFF R has
           a verification layer — an ACTIVE layer when R is implemented, a
           PLANNED layer when R is unimplemented or target-only. Every rule
           (implemented, unimplemented, or target-only) carries a layer.

      (P2) Gap detection: an unimplemented rule with NO planned verification
           layer is a SPEC GAP (not covered). The negative direction is
           load-bearing — silently treating an uncovered unimplemented rule as
           covered would let a realization rule ship with no verification.

    VF-8 is the closure property of the verification stack: it guarantees no
    rule escapes verification. An implemented rule's layer is its active
    verifier; an unimplemented or target-only rule's layer is the planned one;
    a rule with neither is a spec gap that VF-8 surfaces.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the interprocedural_summary engine via a coverage
    check over the rule set (per the proof-checker design sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory
    VF row — unimplemented-rule coverage + cross-call-site provenance summary;
    the foundational-axiom policy sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape — per-node finite
    enumeration over the rule classes).

    Part (P1/P2) — universal-coverage + spec-gap grid:

      The verifier models covered_by_stack(implemented, has_planned_layer) =
      implemented OR has_planned_layer, and is_spec_gap(implemented,
      has_planned_layer) = NOT implemented AND NOT has_planned_layer, and
      asserts both over a grid:
        rl1_implemented_active_layer_covered — implemented + active layer
                                                  -> covered, not a gap.
        rl22_unimplemented_planned_layer_covered — unimplemented RL-22 +
                                                  planned VF-7 layer -> covered.
        ic5_target_only_planned_layer_covered — target-only IC-5 + planned
                                                  VF-2(d)/RL-30 layer -> covered.
        unimplemented_no_layer_spec_gap — unimplemented + no planned
                                                  layer -> SPEC GAP.
      Coverage gate: 4 rules (3 covered + 1 spec gap).

    Negative-direction witness (the gap detection has teeth — an uncovered rule
    is flagged):
      An unimplemented rule with NO planned verification layer is flagged a spec
      gap (covered_by_stack is false, is_spec_gap is true); silently treating it
      as covered would let a realization rule ship without any verification (the
      VF-8 failure mode).

    Engines dispatched:
      interprocedural_summary (PRIMARY — section_09::verify_vf8_stack_applies_to_all_rules;
        universal-coverage + spec-gap detection over the rule-class grid; emits
        Fail on a coverage mismatch or a wrongly-classified spec gap)
      structural_induction (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the
        coverage-manifest VF row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_09 interprocedural_summary engine discharges VF-8 via (P1) universal coverage (every rule has a verification layer — active when implemented, planned when unimplemented/target-only) and (P2) spec-gap detection (an unimplemented rule with no planned layer is a spec gap): 4 rules (implemented RL-1 + unimplemented-planned RL-22 + target-only-planned IC-5 + one uncovered spec gap), with a negative-direction witness flagging the uncovered unimplemented rule
